Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 01:27:15 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 1037/1178] Regenerate from here: semantic_keep keeps a take up
 to a moment, the music goes on anew

A request may carry semantic_keep (the start of a take music codes). The music stage continues
from it: the kept codes follow the prompt in the conditional and unconditional prefixes of that
stage only, the budget shrinks by them, and the song is the kept codes followed by the new ones;
the sound stage keeps the plain prompt. A "Regenerate from..." button in the take card takes the
moment from the player (or asks) and a new music seed. Tested: kept 1:00 of a reading, the first
1500 frames identical, new music after; the sound before 1:00 is rendered again (same codes,
correlation 0.6-0.97 to the old audio), since the sound stage hears each chunk whole.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
